<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phaya Choeng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phaya Choeng is the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tai-lu-people">Tai Lue</a> kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xishuangbanna">Sipsong Panna</a> in the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> valley of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunnan">Yunnan</a>. According to Tai Lue chronicles, he united the Tai principalities of the region in 1180 and founded his capital at Chiang Hung, modern Jinghong. Later rulers of Sipsong Panna traced their line from him.</p></div>
